ograms 2024-2025a.y. Courses offered in Academic Programs 2023-2024a.y. Courses offered in Academic Programs 2022-2023a.y. Courses offered in Academic Programs 2021-2022a.y. Courses offered in Academic Programs 2020-2021a.y. Close Career Services Section Menu Overview Career Guidance & Approaching the Job Market Overview Career Guidance Approaching the Job Market Meet with employers Overview Bespoke events Career fairs JobGate: applying online Your internship: from start to recognition Overview Guide to curricular internships Guide to extracurricular internships Close Breadcrumb Home For Current Students Career Services Contacts Career Services Open share Close Share Close Bocconi Career Services support students and graduates as they enter the job market , providing tools and advice to help them reach their professional goals. Close ties with the business community and organizations have enabled successful partnerships with employers , allowing the recruitment of qualified talents . With the goal of fostering contacts between students and employers worldwide, Bocconi Career Services organize a portfolio of activities related to recruiting, networking and career counseling , available throughout the academic year. Available Career Services Career Guidance & Approaching the Job Market Tools and initiatives to support your first approach to the job market Meet with employers Meet with single employers on bespoke events, or engage with a range of employers during career fairs JobGate: applying online Bocconi\u2019s online portal to find an internship or a job Your internship: from start to credit recognition Activate and manage your internship with the support of Bocconi's Internship Office Placement of Bocconi Graduates 94.7% MSc graduates employed 1 year after graduation 36% employed abroad Bocconi and Employers in 2025 16 career fairs in Italy and abroad, with 700+ participating employers 740+ employers involved in meetings with students and graduates 9,300+ internship and job opportunities posted online Associate Employer network Corporate Associate Program A2A LIFE COMPANY BPER BANCA FERRERO KPMG SAIPEM ACCENTURE CAMPARI GROUP FORVIS MAZARS L\u2019OR\u00c9AL ITALIA SC JOHNSON ALGEBRIS INVESTMENTS CAPGEMINI GE VERNOVA LAZARD SELLA INVESTMENT BANKING ALLIANZ CAPITAL GROUP GENERALI LG ELECTRONICS SIEMENS HEALTHCARE AMAZON CITI GOLDMAN SACHS LIDL ITALIA SIMON KUCHER AMPLIFON CLEARWATER GRIMALDI GROUP LINCOLN INTERNATIONAL SKY ITALIA ANTIN INFRASTRUCTURE PARTNERS CR\u00c9DIT AGRICOLE CIB GRUPPO AXA ITALIA LVMH SNAM ARDIAN CR\u00c9DIT AGRICOLE ITALIA GRUPPO NESTL\u00c9 MCKINSEY & CO. SORGENIA AZIMUT BENETTI GROUP DANONE NUTRICIA GRUPPO PRELIOS MEDIOBANCA STROILI BAIN & COMPANY DE NORA HENKEL MIROGLIO GROUP STELLANTIS BAKER HUGHES DE\u2019 LONGHI GROUP HILTI ITALIA MORGAN STANLEY SYS-DAT GROUP BANCO BPM DECATHLON HINES NEOS TEHA GROUP BANK OF AMERICA DELOITTE HOULIHAN LOKEY NOMURA THE EST\u00c9E LAUDER COMPANIES BARCLAYS DEUTSCHE BANK INTESA SANPAOLO OLIVER WYMAN TOD'S BE MANAGEMENT CONSULTING EDISON IQVIA P&G UBS BENDING SPOONS ENGINEERING J.P. MORGAN PIMCO UNICREDIT BERLIN PACKAGING ENI JAKALA PIRELLI VALUE PARTNERS BIP CONSULTING EQUITA JTI POSTE ITALIANE VENCHI BLACKROCK ESSELUNGA KEARNEY PWC VESTACY BLOOMBERG ETHICA GROUP KERING RECKITT VITALE BNP PARIBAS EVERCORE KITRA ADVISORY ROLAND BERGER WINDTRE BOLTON EY KLECHA & CO. ROTHSCHILD & CO ZURICH INSURANCE EUROPE BOSTON CONSULTING GROUP FASTWEB + VODAFONE Law Firm Associate Program A&O SHEARMAN HOGAN LOVELLS BONELLIEREDE KPMG STUDIO ASSOCIATO - CONSULENZA LEGALE E TRIBUTARIA CHIOMENTI LATHAM & WATKINS CLIFFORD CHANCE LEGANCE DELOITTE TAX&LEGAL PEDERSOLIGATTAI DENTONS PIROLA PENNUTO ZEI & ASSOCIATI DLA PIPER PWC TAX & LEGAL SERVICES AVVOCATI E COMMERCIALISTI EY - TAX&LAW WHITE & CASE GILIBERTI TRISCORNIA E ASSOCIATI ZNR NOTAI Media gallery Bocconi&Jobs Watch video Bocconi&Jobs November 2025 On 12 and 13 November 2025 more than 2800 students and graduates engaged on campus with 146 employers. This adds up to over 1,000 webinar views on 11 November: the University\u2019s flagship career fair reaffirms its relevance in connecting talent with the job market.\n\nAbout #Bocconi&#Jobs\nBocconi&Jobs\u202fis the University's main career fair. It is held twice a year and hosts employers from various countries and sectors, including Auditing, Consulting, Finance, Industrial & Consumer Goods, Services, Law and Tax Firms, Tech.\n\nA unique opportunity to interact with recruiters on-campus, discover internship and job opportunities, and submit your application.\nDiscover more:\n\u27a4 https://www.unibocconi.it/en/current-students/career-services/meet-employers/bocconijobs\n\u27a4 https://www.unibocconi.it/en/employers-and-partners/career-fairs Recruiting Date Arts, Sport & Entertainment Recruiting Date Web & IT Companies Investment Banking Days Bocconi&Jobs abroad Paris Tax & Legal Networking Event Contacts For each initiative you will find a specific contact to ask for more info, if needed. Check the areas above to find the activity of your interest and related contacts. For general information you can contact the Career Service Infopoint: check the FAQ at yoU@B> B in Touch> Career Services and submit your question. Alternatively, you can always reach us through individual appointments at the path: yoU@B> Career Service> Ask for information - book your slot, or through the dedicated number: +39 02 5836.2711. Follow us on LinkedIn Scroll to top Stay in touch Contacts Stay in touch Facebook Linkedin Youtube Instagram Tiktok Weechat Xiaohongshu/RED Listen to our podcast Spotify Spreaker Apple podcast Bocconi Spheres SDA Bocconi School of Management Egea Alumni B4i - Bocconi for innovation yoU@B Agenda Work at Bocconi Media center BTV TL ON Mobile app yoU@B Campus VR Mobile app yoU@B Bocconi shop \u00a9 Universit\u00e0 Bocconi - Via Sarfatti, 25 Milano - PI 03628350153 Footer Privacy Digital accessibility"}, "https://www.unibocconi.it/en/employers-and-partners/jobgate-internship-and-job-posting": {"title": "JobGate: internship and job posting", "description": "JobGate: internship and job posting | Bocconi University Skip to main content What are you looking for? Languages EN IT Menu Close Apply Discover Programs Browse News and Events Giving to Bocconi About Us Overview Organization Quality Assurance Third Mission Ranking International Networks Diversity, Equity and Inclusion Sustainability Community Programs Overview Bachelor of Science Master of Science Law Specialized Masters Programs PhD Summer School SDA Bocconi School of Management Faculty and Research Faculty Departments Research Campus Overview Campus VR Virtual Tour Buildings and Classrooms On-Campus Safety and Security Information Security Library & Archives Bocconi Sport Gallery Applying to Bocconi Overview Bachelor and Law Programs Master of Science and MA Programs Specialized Master Programs PhD Programs Summer School Post-Experience Education News and Events Hub Overview Events ViaSarfatti25 - Our Magazine Research Dissemination For Current Students Overview Welcome Days Bachelor Programs Master of Science and MA Programs Application and Admissions Campus Life Career Services Fees Funding Guidance for MSc Programs Guide to the University Housing Inclusion, Disabilities and Learning Disorders International Mobility IT Education Center Language Center Library & Archives Student Administration Technology and Information Services Timetables, Calendars and Rooms Courses offered in Academic Programs 2026-2027 a.y. For International Students Overview Prospective students - Before your admission Freshly enrolled students - Before you arrive Freshly enrolled students - When you arrive Current students Incoming Exchange Students For Employers and Partners Overview JobGate: internship and job posting Activating and managing internships Career fairs Bespoke events For Alumni Contact us Login Languages EN IT Close menu For Employers and Partners Section Menu Overview JobGate: internship and job posting Activating and managing internships Overview Focus on Curricular vs Extracurricular Internships How to start an internship Career fairs Bespoke events Close JobGate: internship and job posting Section Menu Overview Close Breadcrumb Home For Employers and Partners JobGate: internship and job posting Contacts JobGate: internship and job posting Open share Close Share Close JobGate is Bocconi University's job portal available to employers for posting internship and job offers , managing applications , and accessing the University's graduate database (CVBook). JobGate is also the tool to start internship agreements with selected students and graduates: for info related to this topic, please check the web pages dedicated to internship documents . 2025 wrapped 3,900+ Active companies in JobGate posting offers or hosting internships 9,300+ Internship and job opportunities in Italy or abroad, posted on JobGate Discover more How to register To access JobGate, recruiters need to register at: employers.unibocconi.it During registration, employers need to upload in the system standard information (company name, website, registered and operative office, company contact), as well as a company presentation and a certificate of incorporation (if available). At the end of registration, the recruiter will receive the credentials via email: a contact, either by phone or email, from a Bocconi Account - Employer Relationship Manager, is required to unblock the password and is aimed at sharing the general understanding of the system's functioning, the advertisement publication methods, and the company's recruitment needs. To use this service, the employer must accept the General Conditions that regulate the portal. How to access To access JobGate, recruiters must enter their credentials at: employers.unibocconi.it Passwords are strictly personal and cannot be transferred to third parties. All company contacts needing access to the portal can register by clicking on \"Registration of a new contact\" to obtain their credentials. Posting offers Employers can publish both internship and placement offers. Internship announcements can be dedicated to: Current students (curricular internships) Graduates up to 12 months after graduation (extracurricular internships). For more information on the employer's role and responsibilities in the internship relationship (tutor, internship modality, educational project, etc.), you can visit the pages dedicated to activating and managing internships . Job announcements can be dedicated to: Junior profiles (positions requiring up to 3 years of experience) Senior profiles (positions requiring more than 3 years of experience). The use of JobGate is free, and companies can post as much offers as they wish. The only exception is for Head Hunting Agencies, which can publish job offers for themselves and for client companies only, and internship offers for themselves only: in both cases, the limit is 12 offers per year (maximum of 2 offers simultaneously). CVBook The CVBook Directory is the online database of CVs of Bocconi University graduates . The access is from the JobGate portal, and employers can use filters to sort results according to objective criterias. DAL Project - Disabilities and Work The DAL Service- Disabilities and Work supports companies in identifying and hiring Bocconi students and graduates belonging to Protected Categories. In particular, the service offers the possibility of posting dedicated internship and job offers on JobGate and notifies candidates with the specific requirements . Additionally, Bocconi University has joined C.A.L.D. (Coordinamento Atenei Lombardi per la Disabilit\u00e0) with the aim of undertaking joint initiatives with Lombard universities to sustain the employment of students and graduates with disabilities. Contacts Please check the General Conditions regulating the access and use of the system, as well as the FAQ for a better user experience. For general info: employer.relations@unibocconi.it For tech support: help.jobgate@unibocconi.it Scroll to top Stay in touch Contacts Stay in touch Facebook Linkedin Youtube Instagram Tiktok Weechat Xiaohongshu/RED Listen to our podcast Spotify Spreaker Apple podcast Bocconi Spheres SDA Bocconi School of Management Egea Alumni B4i - Bocconi for innovation yoU@B Agenda Work at Bocconi Media center BTV TL ON Mobile app yoU@B Campus VR Mobile app yoU@B Bocconi shop \u00a9 Universit\u00e0 Bocconi - Via Sarfatti, 25 Milano - PI 03628350153 Footer Privacy Digital accessibility"}, "https://www.unibocconi.it/en/employers-and-partners/career-fairs": {"title": "Career fairs", "description": "Career fairs | Bocconi University Skip to main content What are you looking for? Languages EN IT Menu Close Apply Discover Programs Browse News and Events Giving to Bocconi About Us Overview Organization Quality Assurance Third Mission Ranking International Networks Diversity, Equity and Inclusion Sustainability Community Programs Overview Bachelor of Science Master of Science Law Specialized Masters Programs PhD Summer School SDA Bocconi School of Management Faculty and Research Faculty Departments Research Campus Overview Campus VR Virtual Tour Buildings and Classrooms On-Campus Safety and Security Information Security Library & Archives Bocconi Sport Gallery Applying to Bocconi Overview Bachelor and Law Programs Master of Science and MA Programs Specialized Master Programs PhD Programs Summer School Post-Experience Education News and Events Hub Overview Events ViaSarfatti25 - Our Magazine Research Dissemination For Current Students Overview Welcome Days Bachelor Programs Master of Science and MA Programs Application and Admissions Campus Life Career Services Fees Funding Guidance for MSc Programs Guide to the University Housing Inclusion, Disabilities and Learning Disorders International Mobility IT Education Center Language Center Library & Archives Student Administration Technology and Information Services Timetables, Calendars and Rooms Courses offered in Academic Programs 2026-2027 a.y. For International Students Overview Prospective students - Before your admission Freshly enrolled students - Before you arrive Freshly enrolled students - When you arrive Current students Incoming Exchange Students For Employers and Partners Overview JobGate: internship and job posting Activating and managing internships Career fairs Bespoke events For Alumni Contact us Login Languages EN IT Close menu For Employers and Partners Section Menu Overview JobGate: internship and job posting Activating and managing internships Overview Focus on Curricular vs Extracurricular Internships How to start an internship Career fairs Bespoke events Close Career fairs Section Menu Overview Close Breadcrumb Home For Employers and Partners Career fairs Contacts Career fairs Open share Close Share Close Bocconi's career fairs are one of the main channels through which companies can connect with students and graduates and gain great visibility on campus . Different formats are available, depending on the focus of the events: there are career fairs dedicated to specific sectors or open employers from all fields, or dedicated to particular Countries. In all cases, employers are welcome to showcase their internship and job offers , interact with participants online or in presence, and collect applications . 2025 wrapped 2 editions of Bocconi&Jobs 285 participating employers, 6,200+ participating students and graduates 7 career fairs dedicated to specific business fields 300 participating employers, 4,200+ participating students and graduates 7 editions of Bocconi&Jobs abroad 160+ participating employers, 1300+ participating students and graduates Discover more Bocconi&Jobs: the main career fair With two editions each year, in Spring and Fall, it is the main career fair of the University, open to employers from all business fields and Countries. During the event, companies, organizations, and law firms are welcome to meet students and graduates to promote internship and job opportunities, identify and select ideal profiles, and boost their employer brand. Participation in the event is subject to a fee. For further info: bocconi.jobs@unibocconi.it Bocconi&Jobs abroad: the career fairs dedicated to specific countries Eight editions per year dedicated to speci fic geographical areas: Benelux, DACH, France, Luxembourg, Middle East, Spain and Portugal, UK and Ireland (two editions per year). Th ese career fair s are dedicated to companies offering internship and job opportunities in specific countries. The aim is to facilitate contacts between the local branches of companies and those students interested in internship or job opportunities in some of the main international markets, towards which candidates have a strong motivation. For further info: bocconiandjobsabroad@unibocconi.it Investment Banking Days: the career fair dedicated to Investment Banking Orientation and recruiting event dedicated to the world of Investment Banking, traditionally held at the beginning of the fall semester. The initiative allows companies to join a series of professional guidance activities (career workshops and round tables) to help students better understand the field and prepare for submitting applications. It is also possible to interact with students and graduates and showcase recruiting programs and available opportunities. Participation is reserved for Corporate Associates . For further info: ibw@unibocconi.it Recruiting Dates: the career fairs dedicated to specific business fields Recruiting events dedicated to employers from specific business fields, with the aim to meet students and graduates for networking and promoting available internship and job opportunities. The Recruiting Dates are organized for the following sectors: Arts, Sport & Entertainment; Banking, Financial Services & Fintech; Fashion, Luxury & Beauty; Government, Public Services & International Organizations; Web & IT Companies. For further info: recruiting.date@unibocconi.it Tax&Legal Networking Event: the career fair dedicated to Law & Tax Firms On campus networking and recruiting event, exclusively dedicated to Law Firm Associates . For further info: employer.relations@unibocconi.it Scroll to top Stay in touch Contacts Stay in touch Facebook Linkedin Youtube Instagram Tiktok Weechat Xiaohongshu/RED Listen to our podcast Spotify Spreaker Apple podcast Bocconi Spheres SDA Bocconi School of Management Egea Alumni B4i - Bocconi for innovation yoU@B Agenda Work at Bocconi Media center BTV TL ON Mobile app yoU@B Campus VR Mobile app yoU@B Bocconi shop \u00a9 Universit\u00e0 Bocconi - Via Sarfatti, 25 Milano - PI 03628350153 Footer Privacy Digital accessibility"}, "https://jobmarket.unibocconi.it/": {"error": "RuntimeError: FETCH_FAILURE: Page.goto: net::ERR_NAME_NOT_RESOLVED at https://jobmarket.unibocconi.it/\nCall log:\n  - navigating to \"https://jobmarket.unibocconi.it/\", waiting until \"domcontentloaded\"\n"}, "https://jobmarket.unibocconi.eu/index.php?type=j": {"title": "Job Market", "description": "Job Market - Bocconi University What are you looking for? Languages EN IT Menu Close Apply Discover Programs Browse News and Events Giving to Bocconi About Us Overview Organization Quality Assurance Third Mission Ranking International Networks Diversity, Equity and Inclusion Sustainability Community Programs Overview Bachelor of Science Master of Science Law Specialized Masters Programs PhD Summer School SDA Bocconi School of Management Faculty and Research Faculty Departments Research Campus Overview Campus VR Virtual Tour Buildings and Classrooms On-Campus Safety and Security Information Security Library & Archives Bocconi Sport Gallery Applying to Bocconi Overview Bachelor and Law Programs Master of Science and MA Programs Specialized Master Programs PhD Programs Summer School Post-Experience Education News and Events Hub Overview Events ViaSarfatt